---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DraftNotice from '../../components/DraftNotice.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, DOWNLOAD_URL } from '../../config/site';

const description =
  'Appidge refund policy: a full refund within 14 days of purchase, no questions asked — one email is all it takes. Refunds are returned by Polar, the Merchant of Record, to the original payment method; the license is deactivated once refunded.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Refund Policy" description={description} path="/refund" locale="en">
  <article class="doc">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
      <div class="doc-meta">
        <span><b>Effective</b> <span class="placeholder-slot">[launch date]</span></span>
        <span><b>Last updated</b> 2026-07-23</span>
        <span><b>Applies to</b> Appidge macOS software licenses</span>
      </div>
      <DraftNotice locale="en" updated="2026-07-23" />

      <p class="lede">
        Buy with confidence: <strong>a full refund within 14 days of purchase, no questions
        asked</strong>. One email is all it takes — no justification required, no bank dispute
        needed.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">1</span>How to request one</h2>
      <ol class="steps-inline">
        <li>
          Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}?subject=Refund%20request`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
          with the subject “Refund request”.
        </li>
        <li>
          Include <strong>the email address you used at checkout</strong> and
          <strong>your order number or license key</strong> (both are in your purchase
          confirmation email).
        </li>
        <li>If you like, tell us what went wrong — optional, but it helps us improve.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        You can also review your order and contact support through the
        <strong>Polar customer portal</strong> (linked in your confirmation email). Either way,
        a human will respond — typically within
        <span class="placeholder-slot">[1–2 business days]</span>.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">2</span>How refunds are processed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Polar</strong> is the Merchant of Record for this product. Once your request is
          confirmed, we initiate the refund on Polar's side and the amount is
          <strong>returned to your original payment method</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>Arrival time depends on the payment network and card issuer — usually a few business days.</li>
        <li>
          Once refunded, the corresponding <strong>license is deactivated</strong> and paid
          features stop working on activated devices.
        </li>
        <li>
          As Merchant of Record, Polar may also process eligible refunds directly under its own
          terms; consumer protection prevails.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">3</span>When the 14 days start</h2>
      <p>
        The window runs for 14 calendar days from <strong>the date payment succeeds</strong> on
        the Polar checkout page. Any request within that window qualifies for a full,
        no-questions-asked refund.
      </p>

      <div class="callout good">
        <h3>Better yet: try before you buy</h3>
        <p>
          Download and purchase are separate steps.
          <a href={DOWNLOAD_URL} rel="noopener">Download the free trial</a>, confirm Appidge
          solves your problem, then buy — the best refund is the one you never need.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2><span class="num">4</span>Outside the window, and exceptions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Past 14 days? Contact us anyway. Whether and how much to refund is at our discretion,
          considering the circumstances, applicable law, and Polar's terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          Clear abuse — such as repeated buy-and-refund cycles to avoid paying — may result in
          refused refunds and deactivated licenses.
        </li>
        <li>
          Nothing in this policy limits any <strong>non-waivable consumer rights</strong> under
          the law of your jurisdiction. Where mandatory law grants you better terms, that law
          prevails.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2><span class="num">5</span>Before filing a chargeback, talk to us</h2>
      <p>
        Bank disputes are slow and costly for everyone. For any order issue — duplicate charge,
        accidental purchase, features not matching expectations — email us first; it is almost
        always resolved faster.
      </p>

      <h2><span class="num">6</span>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Refunds and orders: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a><br />
        Operator: <span class="placeholder-slot">[legal entity / sole proprietor name]</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
